    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "To date, the role of TIPS in the preoperative setting of patients requiring elective and emergency surgery remains unclear. Moreover, little quantitative evidence is available to know the number of patients who can undergo surgery after preoperative TIPS and their associated postoperative outcomes; for example, postoperative liver-related events (LRE).",
      "reason": "The manuscript explicitly states the current uncertainty about TIPS' role preoperatively and the lack of quantitative evidence, describing the current state of knowledge and important uncertainties."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "In this systematic review and meta-analysis, we examined the evidence on transjugular intrahepatic portosystemic shunt (TIPS) as a bridge to elective and emergency surgery in cirrhotic patients. We aimed to assess the perioperative characteristics, management approaches, and outcomes of this intervention, which is used to achieve portal decompression and enable the safe performance of elective and emergent surgery.",
      "reason": "The abstract explains the aims and rationale for conducting the review, stating the purpose and clinical importance of assessing TIPS to enable safe surgery in cirrhotic patients."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No retrieved evidence discusses the existence of prior similar systematic reviews or explains the need for this review as an update or replication, nor cites previous reviews."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "the intervention, which is used to achieve portal decompression and enable the safe performance of elective and emergent surgery.",
      "reason": "The abstract briefly describes the proposed mechanism of action of TIPS (portal decompression) and how that enables safe performance of surgery."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No retrieved evidence presents or refers to a logic model showing hypothesised relationships between intervention components and outcomes."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 85
}

{
